 ## Proof
 
-1.1 Fix $z$ with $p_Z(z)>0$ and write $q_{xy}=p_{XY|z}(x,y)$, $q_x=\sum_yq_{xy}$; for $q_x>0$ define $q_{y|x}=q_{xy}/q_x$. By [F4], these are pmfs and $q_{xy}=q_xq_{y|x}$ on positive support. Expanding the logarithm gives $-\sum_{q_{xy}>0}q_{xy}\ln q_{xy}=-\sum_{q_x>0,y}q_xq_{y|x}(\ln q_x+\ln q_{y|x})$. Since $\sum_yq_{y|x}=1$, the first sum is $-\sum_{q_x>0}q_x\ln q_x$ and the second is $\sum_{q_x>0}q_x(-\sum_{q_{y|x}>0}q_{y|x}\ln q_{y|x})$, exactly $H(q_X)+\sum_xq_xH(q_{Y|x})$ by [F5]. Weighting this equality by $p_Z(z)$ and summing over positive-mass $z$ using [F1] proves $H(X,Y|Z)=H(X|Z)+H(Y|X,Z)$. Zero atoms contribute zero by convention. [F1, F4, F5, given, algebra]
+1.1 Fix $z$ with $p_Z(z)>0$ and write $q_{xy}=p_{XY|z}(x,y)$, $q_x=\sum_yq_{xy}$; for $q_x>0$ define $q_{y|x}=q_{xy}/q_x$. By [F4], these are pmfs and $q_{xy}=q_xq_{y|x}$ on positive support. On the positive support both factors are positive, so the product law [F6] gives $-\sum_{q_{xy}>0}q_{xy}\ln q_{xy}=-\sum_{q_x>0,y}q_xq_{y|x}(\ln q_x+\ln q_{y|x})$. Since $\sum_yq_{y|x}=1$, the first sum is $-\sum_{q_x>0}q_x\ln q_x$ and the second is $\sum_{q_x>0}q_x(-\sum_{q_{y|x}>0}q_{y|x}\ln q_{y|x})$, exactly $H(q_X)+\sum_xq_xH(q_{Y|x})$ by [F5]. Weighting this equality by $p_Z(z)$ and summing over positive-mass $z$ using [F1] proves $H(X,Y|Z)=H(X|Z)+H(Y|X,Z)$. Zero atoms contribute zero by convention. [F1, F4, F5, F6, given, algebra]
 
